 "plain_temperature": "Over Egypt, NASA's station record (GISTEMP, 250 km) warms +0.42 °C per decade from 2001 to 2025; our NASA POWER cells in the same 32 areas of 2 by 2 degrees warm +0.24. Both records go the same way in 32 of 32 areas and their yearly values move together (median correlation 0.92). With the same test, the station record proves the warming in 30 of 32 areas, POWER in 12: POWER (a weather model, MERRA-2) shows weaker warming than the thermometers over Egypt, so many 'not proven' cells in our maps are too cautious, not a sign that Egypt is not warming.",
 "plain_rain": "Rain: POWER over Egypt is 2.6 times higher after 2015 than before (16 mm to 41 mm a year). NASA's GPCP record (satellites and rain gauges) at the same places changes by 1.24 times (30 mm to 37 mm). The jump is in the POWER record, not in real rain, so the crop projections take this one-time step out of rain, humidity and soil wetness before measuring their trend, and continue that trend from today's level."
}